* dev180 -- BRING-UP MODELS ONLY. NOT A CALIBRATED PROCESS.
*
* Hand-written BSIM3v3.3 cards with parameters in the right ballpark for a
* generic 180nm bulk CMOS process. They exist so the harness can be developed
* and tested without a multi-gigabyte PDK download, and so CI has something
* deterministic to run against.
*
* These are NOT foundry models. Threshold voltages, mobilities and capacitances
* are approximate and uncorrelated with any real fab. `PDK.calibrated` is False
* for this process and bias/bench.py refuses to emit publishable results with
* it. Use sky130 or ihp-sg13g2 for anything you intend to report.

.model nch nmos level=8 version=3.3.0
+ tnom=27 tox=4.1e-9 xj=1.0e-7 nch=2.3e17
+ vth0=0.39 k1=0.53 k2=0.029 k3=0.0
+ dvt0=1.3 dvt1=0.53 dvt2=-0.032
+ u0=280 ua=-1.2e-9 ub=2.3e-18 uc=5.6e-11
+ vsat=1.05e5 a0=1.0 ags=0.28 a1=0.0 a2=1.0
+ rdsw=250 prwg=0.5 prwb=0.0 wr=1.0
+ nfactor=1.1 cit=0.0 cdsc=2.4e-4 cdscd=0.0 cdscb=0.0
+ eta0=0.045 etab=-0.07 dsub=0.56
+ pclm=1.2 pdiblc1=0.24 pdiblc2=0.0088 pdiblcb=-0.005 drout=0.56
+ pscbe1=4.2e8 pscbe2=1.0e-5 pvag=0.0 delta=0.01
+ mobmod=1 prt=0.0 ute=-1.5
+ kt1=-0.11 kt1l=0.0 kt2=0.022 ua1=4.3e-9 ub1=-7.6e-18 uc1=-5.6e-11
+ at=3.3e4 wl=0.0 ww=0.0 wwl=0.0 ll=0.0 lw=0.0 lwl=0.0
+ capmod=2 xpart=0.5
+ cgdo=3.9e-10 cgso=3.9e-10 cgbo=1.0e-12
+ cj=1.0e-3 pb=0.8 mj=0.35 cjsw=2.0e-10 pbsw=0.8 mjsw=0.2
+ js=1.0e-8 jsw=0.0

.model pch pmos level=8 version=3.3.0
